  "question": {
    "text": "A chloro compound &quot;A&quot;.<br />(i) forms aldehydes on ozonolysis followed by the hydrolysis.<br />(ii) when vaporized completely <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>53</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>448</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of vapour at STP. The number of carbon atoms in a molecule of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>448</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of A gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>53</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>53</mn></mrow><mn>448</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>22400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mi>Zn</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math> (aldehyde)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>-carbon atoms and molecular mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>",
